messages:    6%|5         | 12/204 [00:00<00:11, 16.83it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Black Mirror" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Karen will share \'Black Mirror\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1.**Identify the relevant information:**\n   - "Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.\n   - If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.\n   - If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.\n   - Karen does not download "Black Mirror".\n   - "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.\n   - If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n2.**Analyze the implications:**\n   - Since "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show and Karen does not download it, we can infer that Karen does not binge-watch "Black Mirror".The statement "If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa" implies that Karen shares a Netflix show even if she doesn\'t binge-watch it.\nSince Karen does not binge-watch "Black Mirror", she will still share it to Lisa.\n\n3.**Conclusion:**\nBased on the given information, Karen will share "Black Mirror" to Lisa.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n**A) True**\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
