h a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n3.**Determine the implications for Luke:**.\n   - Since Luke either is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he is neither a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members, we need to consider both scenarios:.\n     - **Scenario 1:** Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members.\n       - According to the context, if people are twins or triplets, they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.\n       - Therefore, Luke spends a lot of time hanging out and playing with his siblings.Luke spends a lot of time hanging out and playing with his siblings, regardless of whether he is a twin or triplet and has strong bonds with his family members.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
