messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people perform in school talent shows often, then they attend and are very engaged with school events. People either perform in school talent shows often or are inactive and disinterested members of their community. If people chaperone high school dances, then they are not students who attend the school. All people who are inactive and disinterested members of their community chaperone high school dances. All young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school. Bonnie either both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, or she neither attends and is very engaged with school events nor is a student who attends the school.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If Bonnie is either both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances or neither is a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities, then Bonnie is either a student who attends the school or is an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine the truth value of the statement, let\'s break down the information provided and analyze it step by step:\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:\n   - People who perform in school talent shows often are very engaged with school events.\n   - People who are inactive and disinterested members of their community either do not perform in school talent shows often or do not attend school events.\n   - People who chaperone high school dances are not students who attend the school.\n   - All young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school.\n   - Bonnie either both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, or she neither attends and is very engaged with school events nor is a student who attends the school.\n\n2.**Statement Breakdown**:\n   - The statement to evaluate is: "If Bonnie is either both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances or neither is a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities, then Bonnie is either a student who attends the school or is an inactive and disinterested member of the community."\n\n3.**Logical Reasoning**:\n   - We need to consider two scenarios for Bonnie:\n     1.Bonnie is a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances.\n     2.Bonnie is neither a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities.\n\n4.**Scenario 1**:\n   - If Bonnie is a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances:\n     - According to the context, people who chaperone high school dances are not students who attend the school.\n     - Therefore, Bonnie cannot be a student who attends the school.\n     - Since Bonnie is a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities, she must be a student who attends the school.\n     - However, this contradicts the fact that she is not a student who attends the school.\n     - Hence, this scenario is logically inconsistent.If Bonnie is either a young child or teenager who aspires to advance her academic career and educational opportunities, then she is a dedicated student who actively participates in school activities and events. Therefore, she cannot be considered an inactive or disinterested member of the community. This interpretation contradicts the context provided.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 52%|#####2    | 107/204 [00:20<00:09, 10.69it/s]
