messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1.**Identify the relevant information:**\n   - "Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.\n   - If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.\n   - If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.\n   - Karen does not download "Black Mirror".\n   - "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.\n   - If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n2.**Analyze the given information:**\n   - Since "Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show, according to the first piece of information, Karen will binge-watch "Stranger Things".\n   - However, the second piece of information states that if and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.Since Karen downloads "Black Mirror", which is also a popular Netflix show, we can infer that Karen binge-watches "Black Mirror".\n   - Therefore, Karen binge-watches "Stranger Things" because she downloads "Black Mirror".\n\n3.**Conclusion:**\n   - Since Karen binge-watches "Stranger Things", she will share it to Lisa.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:\n**A) True**\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
