ty deposit is no more than $1500**: This condition states that Tom will rent an apartment in a managed building only if he is allowed to move in with his cat Fluffy and the security deposit is no more than $1500.\n\nNow, let\'s evaluate the given statement:\n\n- The Olive Garden is an unmanaged building.\n- The monthly rent at The Olive Garden is not $2000.\n- The security deposit cannot be $2000 or more than $2000.\n- Tom does not have a cat named Fluffy, which is not a pet.\n- Tom will not rent an apartment in a managed building if he is allowed to move in with Fluffy and the security deposit is more than $1500.\n\nSince the security deposit cannot be $2000 or more than $2000, and Tom will only rent an apartment in a managed building if the security deposit is more than $1500, it is certain that Tom will not rent an apartment in The Olive Garden. The security deposit cannot be $2000 or more than $2000, and we have enough information to determine it is not exactly $1500.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n<answer>D) Certain</answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
