messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock does not have wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Rock does not have wings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, we need to analyze each piece of information step by step.\n\n1.**All mammals are animals.**.\n   - This means that any animal that is a mammal does not necessarily have wings.\n\n2.**All monkeys are mammals.**.\n   - This implies that all monkeys are animals and are part of the mammal category.\n\n3.**An animal is either a monkey or a bird.**.\n   - This statement does not directly relate to the presence or absence of wings in animals.\n\n4.**All birds fly.**.\n   - This indicates that any bird has the ability to fly.\n\n5.**All animals breathe.**.\n   - This means that any animal, including those that do not fly, can breathe.\n\n6.**If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.**.\n   - This statement is a conditional statement that suggests if Rock is not a bird or a fly, then it cannot fly or breathe.Rock does have wings, as all birds fly.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
